		<title type="html"><![CDATA[COLLADA Physics and Bullet at GDC 2007]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=3718#p3718"><![CDATA[
In case you are interested: I'll be giving an overview of COLLADA Physics capabilities and tools and show some demos using Bullet at the Game Developers Conference 2007 in San Francisco.<br><br>This will happen at the Khronos booth at Thursday March 8 from 16:00 - 16:25<br><a href="http://www.khronos.org/library/detail/gdc_2007_collada" class="postlink">Download</a> COLLADA Physics presentation at Khronos.org website.<br><br>Also at the Sony booth, Wednesday morning (10-12 AM) and Friday morning (11-12 AM) there are some COLLADA Physics and basic Bullet demos running on Playstation 3.<br><br>Thanks,<br>Erwin<br><br>By the way, this includes demonstrations of some of the Rube Goldberg machines that contestants have been submitting for <a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/mediawiki-1.5.8/index.php?title=PhysicsContest2007" class="postlink">the physics contest</a>.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Sat Mar 03, 2007 3:33 am</p><hr />
